  "difficulty_reason": "Supplying the named Brenier existence, smooth regularity, Caffarelli contraction and standard heat-semigroup prerequisites leaves a new source-local regularity mechanism under a Laplacian bound rather than directional Hessian bounds. The proof replaces directional differences by spherical averages, establishes finite integrals and a cofactor integration-by-parts inequality with cutoff boundary terms controlled uniformly, and closes the sharp Lp-to-Linfinity estimate. The required original core then constructs curvature-preserving Ornstein-Uhlenbeck approximations and passes the distributional Laplacian bound to the full-support limit, including complete AppendixA proofs; this is above qualification PDE/optimal transport.",
